ROUTINE Adjudicate
 ; ============================================================================
 ; do ^Adjudicate -- when the classifier and the catalogue disagree, work out
 ; which one is right.
 ; ============================================================================
 ;
 ; THE PROBLEM
 ;
 ; ^Classify trains on ESA's published labels and then disagrees with them on
 ; 656 of 17,597 held-out sources. Both parties looked at the same light curve
 ; and reached different answers, so the light curve cannot settle it. The
 ; tie-breaker has to come from outside both.
 ;
 ; Disagreement is not random, which is the first evidence that both are
 ; tracking something real:
 ;
 ;     ESA best_class_score   disagreement rate
 ;     0.0 - 0.2                    7.9%
 ;     0.2 - 0.4                    4.1%
 ;     0.4 - 0.6                    2.8%
 ;     0.6 - 0.8                    1.9%
 ;     0.8 - 1.0                    0.8%
 ;
 ; A tenfold gradient. The two agree where the physics is clear and diverge
 ; exactly where the catalogue was already unsure.
 ;
 ; TWO DIFFERENT DISAGREEMENT COUNTS, AND WHICH ONE MEANS SOMETHING
 ;
 ; The 656 above is measured offline on a held-out quarter of the labelled
 ; sources, so those are predictions on data the model never saw. That is the
 ; number the rates in the table come from and the one worth reasoning about.
 ;
 ; Running this routine reports about 63. GaiaVariableScored carries a
 ; var_class only for the 10,660 sources in the committed training extract, and
 ; the model agrees with itself on 99.4% of the rows it was fitted on, so what
 ; is left is its residual training error rather than a hard case. Expect the
 ; in-database verdicts to favour the catalogue for the same reason: a source
 ; the model gets wrong on its own training data is usually a source the model
 ; is wrong about.
 ;
 ; Scoring the unlabelled 64,408 would find real disagreements, but there is
 ; nothing to disagree with -- no published label -- so they cannot be counted
 ; without pulling more of vari_classifier_result over TAP.
 ;
 ; THREE STAGES, CHEAPEST FIRST
 ;
 ; Nothing reaches a language model that arithmetic could have settled.
 ;
 ;  1. SQL -- find the disagreements.
 ;
 ;  2. numpy/sklearn (gaia_dispute.py) -- settle what distance can settle.
 ;     Compare each disputed source to the centroids of confidently-agreed
 ;     examples of both classes: 64.3% sit closer to the classifier's answer.
 ;     Then k-means over the disputed sources, which collapses ~50 label pairs
 ;     into 6 recurring degeneracies and merges the bidirectional ones
 ;     (RS->ECL and ECL->RS are one phenomenon) without being told they are
 ;     related. Five lines of numpy, deterministic, free, and better at this
 ;     than an agent would be.
 ;
 ;  3. The literature (gaia_simbad.py + Gaia.Adjudicator / Gaia.LiteratureAudit)
 ;     -- what survives stages 1 and 2 is genuinely textual, and it is the only
 ;     part that needs an LLM. Ranking a 2017 machine-learned identification
 ;     against 2022 survey photometry means knowing how those methods compare,
 ;     which is knowledge held in prose and absent from every table here.
 ;
 ; THE CIRCULARITY TRAP
 ;
 ; SIMBAD ingests the Gaia DR3 variability catalogue itself. Across all of
 ; SIMBAD, 61.6% of EB*, 38.6% of LP* and 32.1% of RR* classifications
 ; originate from bibcode 2022yCat.1358....0G -- which is the label source this
 ; project trains on. Treating those as independent evidence would mean
 ; checking ESA's labels with ESA's labels and finding, unsurprisingly, that
 ; ESA agrees with itself. Every object-type query filters that bibcode out.
 ; On these 656 disputes it accounts for 159 of 1,412 rows (11.3%); the
 ; remaining 88.7% are genuinely independent.
 ;
 ; FLAT CALL OR RECURSION
 ;
 ; Most disputed sources carry a handful of papers and one Chat() call sees all
 ; of them (Gaia.Adjudicator). Well-studied stars do not: HD 283572 has 311
 ; references, 72 relevant. Truncating to the top 20 by keyword score means a
 ; heuristic that has never read the papers decides which ones the model sees --
 ; and that heuristic was wrong here once already, matching galactic rotation
 ; curves and maser kinematics on "rotation" and displacing a 1993 paper with
 ; the star's own name in the title. Fixing it changed the verdict.
 ;
 ; So above 25 relevant papers the bibliography becomes a SQL table and
 ; Gaia.LiteratureAudit recurses over it (rlm-core): the root peeks at
 ; aggregates across epoch, claim type and targeted-vs-survey, picks a
 ; decomposition, and each leaf reads only its slice. Nothing is dropped and
 ; context depth stays constant.
 ;
 ; WORKED EXAMPLE
 ;
 ;     Gaia DR3 164536250037820160 = HD 283572
 ;       catalogue : YSO  (ESA confidence 0.29)
 ;       model     : RS   (classifier confidence 0.64)
 ;       colour 1.06 against typical YSO 3.13 and typical RS 1.41
 ;       SIMBAD: G5IVe, 311 references, 72 relevant, 39 of them about rotation
 ;
 ;     verdict: both defensible -- a young star that is also a spotted rotator
 ;
 ; Which is right. Papers from 1984 onward describe the rotational modulation
 ; the classifier detected, and the star is a confirmed young stellar object.
 ; A single-label catalogue cannot record both.
 ;
 ; COVERAGE
 ;
 ; 337 of the 656 disputes (51.4%) have a SIMBAD entry at all. For the other
 ; 319 the verdict is "insufficient evidence" and no LLM call is spent.
 ;
 ; REQUIREMENTS
 ;
 ; Network access to SIMBAD (CDS) and OPENAI_API_KEY for the agent stage.
 ; Without the key the deterministic stages still run and the verdicts say the
 ; agent was unavailable. Kept out of ^RunScript for the same reason as
 ; ^Analyze: LLM and network latency are not ours to control.
 ;
 ; Optional argument: one source_id to adjudicate on its own. Otherwise the
 ; most confident disagreements are taken first, because those are the cases
 ; where the classifier is making a real claim rather than guessing.
 ; ============================================================================
 New inDir,outDir,startTime,cmd,rc,elapsed,extra
 Set inDir = "/home/irisowner/dev/data/in"
 Set outDir = "/home/irisowner/dev/data/out"
 Do ##class(%File).CreateDirectoryChain(outDir)
 Set extra = $Get(%1, "")
 Set startTime = $ZHOROLOG
 Set cmd = "GAIA_CACHE="_inDir_" GAIA_OUT="_outDir_" /usr/irissys/bin/irispython /home/irisowner/dev/adjudicate_disputes.py"
 If extra '= "" { Set cmd = cmd_" --source "_extra }
 Set rc = $ZF(-1, cmd)
 Set elapsed = $ZHOROLOG - startTime
 If rc '= 0 { Write "ERROR: rc=",rc,! Quit }
 Write "OK: ",outDir,"/disputes.json",!
 Write "Elapsed time: ",elapsed," seconds",!
 Quit
